{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>For any man who has a blemish shall not come near.</b> It is not fitting that he should come near — as in ״הַקְרִיבֵהוּ נָא לְפֶחָתֶךָ״ (Malachi 1)." "<b>Charim.</b> One whose nose is sunken between the two eyes, so that he appears to paint both eyes as one (Sifra; Bekhorot 43)." "<b>Sarua.</b> One whose limbs are unequal — one eye large and one eye small, or one leg longer than its fellow (Sifra; Bekhorot 40)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:35.421174217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}